From 29b300b347573674a4da27860c0369af0e9f6ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:11:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): forge control tri-state for gates/rails +
 guarantee matrix + locus badges (B6)

Adds the control-plane guarantee matrix and an honesty-enforcing control
surface so the cockpit never sells enforcement Forge cannot deliver.

- docs/reference/control-plane-guarantees.md: the contract badges read from --
  state (mandatory/optional/permission) x enforcement-locus (run-time-deny gate|
  rail|permission vs render-time presence-only for mcp/rules/skills).
- lib/control-plane.js: pure taxonomy (classify surface, derive state, locus,
  badge, plan write-intent). Single source of truth for the matrix.
- forge control <id> <state>: tri-state ONLY for gate.*/rail.*, reusing the ONE
  resolver-enforced field workflow.gates.<id>.enabled (no fake parallel key).
  REFUSES mcp/rules/skills + permission-on-non-human + optional-on-locked with a
  guarantee-matrix pointer. forge control status renders the all-surface read.
- forge options gates: decorated with enforcement-locus badges (724356ea).

Reuses the existing gate/rail toggle mechanism so setting a state is genuinely
honored at run time (asserted via getResolvedRuntimeGraph). Deferred by design:
control for advisory surfaces (mcp/rules/skills) has no run-time deny path.

Issues: 7dc59af2 (controls + forge control), 724356ea (all-surface read + badges)
Epic: 363954dd

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
